From: crosshatch-player <dlab-g3@local>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Stop a bit pointer that passed the VLC data, and fail the decode

JPEGGetMoreData moves the VLC data down and refills once a MCU ends past
FILE_HIGHWATER (1536), but returns at once when the bit pointer has already
passed the data in the buffer (iVLCOff > iVLCSize): a colour MCU of long codes
(3 blocks at 4:4:4, 6 at 4:2:0, up to about 248 bytes each) started under the
mark can end past the 2 KiB buffer, and from then on no refill ever moves the
pointer back, so every later MCU reads further past ucFileBuf. This sets the
pointer to the end of the data, records JPEG_DECODE_ERROR, and DecodeJPEG ends
its MCU loops on it (they stop at iErr). Found by the gray viewer's host
decoder tests (test/game_display_lab); applied with 0001-0003 by
scripts/patch_jpegdec.py and test/game_display_lab/CMakeLists.txt.

---
--- a/src/jpeg.inl
+++ b/src/jpeg.inl
@@ -1546,7 +1546,17 @@
     int iDelta = pPage->iVLCSize - pPage->iVLCOff;
 //    printf("Getting more data...size=%d, off=%d\n", pPage->iVLCSize, pPage->iVLCOff);
     // move any existing data down
-    if (iDelta >= (JPEG_FILE_BUF_SIZE-64) || iDelta < 0)
+    if (iDelta < 0)
+    {
+        // CrossPoint patch: a MCU larger than the room past FILE_HIGHWATER (a colour MCU of long codes) took the bit
+        // pointer past the data in the buffer. Returning here as before left it there for good, every later MCU
+        // moving it further past ucFileBuf: stop it at the data's end and fail the decode (DecodeJPEG stops at it).
+        pPage->iVLCOff = pPage->iVLCSize;
+        pPage->bb.pBuf = &pPage->ucFileBuf[pPage->iVLCSize];
+        pPage->iError = JPEG_DECODE_ERROR;
+        return;
+    }
+    if (iDelta >= (JPEG_FILE_BUF_SIZE-64))
         return; // buffer is already full; no need to read more data
     if (pPage->iVLCOff != 0)
     {
@@ -5365,7 +5375,12 @@
             } // if there is a restart interval
             // See if we need to feed it more data
             if (pJPEG->iVLCOff >= FILE_HIGHWATER)
+            {
                 JPEGGetMoreData(pJPEG); // need more 'filtered' VLC data
+                // CrossPoint patch: the bit pointer had passed the buffer's data; the decode ends here.
+                if (pJPEG->iError == JPEG_DECODE_ERROR)
+                    iErr = JPEG_DECODE_ERROR;
+            }
         } // for x
     } // for y
     if (iErr != 0)
